.TH LIFE 1
.SH NAME
life \- cellular automaton demo, per-pixel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/life
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Life
is a port of the TempleOS graphics demo
.BR Life.HC ,
a cellular automaton run per-pixel on a 640x480 board.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
The board starts empty.
Hold button 1 and drag to draw green lines of live cells;
the line thickness follows the mouse speed, so fast strokes are
fat and slow ones thin.
Drawing restarts the generation in progress from the modified
board, and the simulation keeps running while you draw.
.PP
The rule is the demo's own variant, not classic Conway:
counting the 3x3 neighbourhood
.I including
the cell itself, a live cell survives when the count is 3 and a
dead cell is born when the count is 2.
The border pixels are permanently dead; there is no wraparound.
A new generation is computed roughly every 50 milliseconds.
.PP
Any key that produces a character exits.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/life.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
.SH BUGS
The original runs fullscreen and borderless; this is an ordinary
640x480 window.
